From: Yanghan Ye <yyh94306@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] wifi: mt76: mix NPU flow hash for RPS

The NPU descriptor supplies a 16-bit PPE flow-table index. Publishing it
as an L4 skb hash prevents software hash calculation, but RPS selects a
CPU using the upper bits of a 32-bit hash through reciprocal_scale().
Every 16-bit value therefore selects the first CPU in a multi-CPU RPS
map, concentrating host receive work and its backlog on that CPU.

Mix the flow-table index with jhash_1word() before setting the skb hash,
matching the existing Airoha Ethernet receive path. Keep the original
16-bit index for PPE flow binding and retain per-flow hash stability.

Fixes: 141a81557070 ("wifi: mt76: Introduce the NPU generic layer")
Signed-off-by: Yanghan Ye <yyh94306@gmail.com>
--- a/npu.c
+++ b/npu.c
@@ -3,6 +3,7 @@
  * Copyright (c) 2025 AIROHA Inc
  * Author: Lorenzo Bianconi <lorenzo@kernel.org>
  */
+#include <linux/jhash.h>
 #include <linux/kernel.h>
 #include <net/flow_offload.h>
 #include <net/pkt_cls.h>
@@ -204,7 +205,7 @@ void mt76_npu_check_ppe(struct mt76_dev
 		goto out;
 
 	hash = FIELD_GET(NPU_RX_DMA_FOE_ID_MASK, info);
-	skb_set_hash(skb, hash, PKT_HASH_TYPE_L4);
+	skb_set_hash(skb, jhash_1word(hash, 0), PKT_HASH_TYPE_L4);
 
 	reason = FIELD_GET(NPU_RX_DMA_CRSN_MASK, info);
 	if (reason == PPE_CPU_REASON_HIT_UNBIND_RATE_REACHED) {
